@startuml
title S3 - Carry out or cancel a dispatch task (UC-M4-03, UC-M4-04): proposed interaction contract
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide footbox
actor Operator
participant "Sensor / iot_sim" as Sensor
boundary UI
control Allocation
control Core
control Reservation
Operator -> UI: Confirm pick-up at source Hub
UI -> Allocation: start_task(task_id)
Allocation -> Allocation: Check task is Approved
Allocation -> Core: Pick up the reserved vehicle (Reservation port)
Core --> Allocation: Vehicle InUse, source space released
Allocation -> Allocation: Task InProgress; log
Operator -> UI: Confirm return at destination Hub
UI -> Allocation: complete_task(task_id)
group Atomic unit of work (NFR-09)
  Allocation -> Core: Return vehicle to the held destination space
  Core -> Reservation: Consume the hold, complete the system reservation
end
Core --> Allocation: Vehicle Returned; Available after the normal readiness step
Allocation -> Allocation: Task Completed; log
Allocation --> UI: Completed
== Alternative paths (instead of the normal flow above) ==
alt Vehicle missing, faulty, or task timed out
  Sensor -> Core: Fault event (or clock tick past the timeout)
  Core -> Allocation: Domain event
  Allocation -> Core: Release held vehicle and space
  Allocation -> Allocation: Task Failed; start re-plan (UC-M4-08)
else Operator cancels (task Approved or InProgress)
  Operator -> UI: Cancel with reason
  UI -> Allocation: cancel_task(task_id, reason)
  alt Vehicle already at the destination
    Allocation -> Allocation: Complete the task for that vehicle (no move back)
  else Vehicle not yet delivered
    Allocation -> Core: Release held vehicle and space
    Allocation -> Allocation: Task Cancelled; log
  end
end
@enduml
